399
00:22:27.489 --> 00:22:30.945
Context, Hourly scripts with 50 threads got us blocked.

400
00:22:31.225 --> 00:22:33.956
Duplicate URLs wasted half the fetches.

401
00:22:34.236 --> 00:22:36.689
The re-crawl policy ignored change rates.

402
00:22:36.969 --> 00:22:39.508
A redesign published 0 rupeesprices.

403
00:22:40.858 --> 00:22:46.021
Decision, Mercator-style frontier with per-host back queues and adaptive politeness.

404
00:22:46.301 --> 00:22:48.327
Hosts are partitioned across nodes.

405
00:22:48.607 --> 00:22:54.133
URLs are canonicalised with site rules and stored as a 64-bit fingerprint set.

406
00:22:54.413 --> 00:23:00.535
Re-crawl uses price-based change-rate estimates with priors and value weights, plus a uniform floor.

407
00:23:00.815 --> 00:23:03.802
Sitemaps and robots.txt are first-class.

408
00:23:04.082 --> 00:23:08.967
Extraction prefers JSON-LD, with validation, quarantine and canaries.

409
00:23:09.247 --> 00:23:10.698
Legal review per site.

410
00:23:12.048 --> 00:23:25.360
Related ADRs, ADR-390 Frontier: per-host queues, ready-host heap, default 1 request or 2 s per site, Retry-After honoured, circuit breaker at 5% errors (L1).

411
00:23:25.640 --> 00:23:36.200
ADR-391 Dedup: canonical URL rules per site, exact 64-bit fingerprints (no Bloom filters for tracked pages) (L2).

412
00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:52.373
ADR-392 Re-crawl: every page at least every 72 h; the remaining budget uses optimal allocation on continuously updated estimates with category priors; flash-deal list weighted times 5 (L3).

413
00:23:52.653 --> 00:24:02.019
ADR-393 Discovery: sitemaps + robots.txt; template budgets; soft-404 detection (L4).

414
00:24:02.299 --> 00:24:11.003
ADR-394 Legal: public pages only, identified UA, no circumvention, per-site approval recorded.

415
00:24:11.283 --> 00:24:12.243
Requirements.

416
00:24:13.593 --> 00:24:14.425
R1:

417
00:24:14.705 --> 00:24:17.329
Zero requests above a site's configured rate.

418
00:24:17.609 --> 00:24:21.555
429s below 0.1% of fetches.

419
00:24:21.835 --> 00:24:30.603
R2: ≥ 90% of tracked prices current (time-averaged); flash-deal pages ≥ 80%.

420
00:24:30.883 --> 00:24:31.737
R3:

421
00:24:32.017 --> 00:24:34.214
No invalid price is ever published.

422
00:24:34.494 --> 00:24:37.417
An extraction failure alerts within 15 minutes.

423
00:24:37.697 --> 00:24:38.593
R4:

424
00:24:38.873 --> 00:24:42.585
New products on sitemaps are discovered within 24 hours.

425
00:24:42.865 --> 00:24:43.739
R5:

426
00:24:44.019 --> 00:24:46.878
A per-site kill switch takes effect in under a minute.

427
00:24:47.158 --> 00:24:48.566
Decisions in detail.

428
00:24:49.916 --> 00:24:54.972
Frontier (ADR-390): hosts are consistent-hashed to 8 nodes.

429
00:24:55.252 --> 00:25:00.799
Each node keeps back queues in memory, persisted to RocksDB, and the host heap in memory.

430
00:25:01.079 --> 00:25:03.532
Dedup (ADR-391):

431
00:25:03.812 --> 00:25:11.257
64-bit xxHash of the canonical URL, kept in a partitioned hash set with a Redis-backed snapshot.

432
00:25:11.537 --> 00:25:19.495
Scheduling (ADR-392): change events update the estimates, and a nightly job recomputes allocations.

433
00:25:19.775 --> 00:25:24.191
The job scheduler (Ch 50) fires due fetches through the frontier.

434
00:25:24.471 --> 00:25:31.063
Discovery (ADR-393): a daily sitemap diff feeds new URLs to the frontier.

435
00:25:32.413 --> 00:25:38.813
Legal (ADR-394): a site config can't be enabled without a recorded approval.

436
00:25:39.093 --> 00:25:40.117
Consequences.

437
00:25:40.397 --> 00:25:47.031
Costs: per-site configuration and extractor maintenance, legal reviews, and estimation infrastructure.

438
00:25:47.311 --> 00:25:54.757
Benefits: no blocks, no wasted duplicate fetches, fresher prices where they matter, and no 0 rupeesincidents.

